# Android signing
# key.properties + release keystores are per-developer secrets — never
# commit them. The one exception is **/android/keystore/debug.keystore:
# a *debug* keystore signs nothing distributable, so committing it is
# standard practice (not a secret leak) and is what makes assetlinks.json,
# passkey origins, and any other certificate-bound feature work identically
# for every developer and CI runner instead of only whoever's machine
# generated AGP's implicit ~/.android/debug.keystore first
# (Archipelago-a71b). See .well-known/README.md.
key.properties
*.jks
**/android/keystore/*.keystore
!**/android/keystore/debug.keystore

